{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/406277-assassin-s-creed-ideal-lunar-inspiration","id":406277,"title":"Assassin's Creed - Ideal Lunar Inspiration","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-14T19:38:41-08:00","id":406277,"title":"Assassin's Creed - Ideal Lunar Inspiration","content":"I've come to the conclusion that the Assassin's Creed series is your one-stop shop for Full Moon or Changing Moon Lunar inspiration. Given that I've never known anyone to play anything besides a Full Moon, right now that makes it ideal for Lunars as a whole until their 3e replacements come out.<br /> <br /> Consider the following: The Assassin Order has fought for centuries against the tyranny of the Templars, public figures in positions of public power (the dynasts) who are also agents of a shadowy conspiracy (the Sidereals). The Assassins have survived as long as they have by being elusive, secretive, and extremely adaptable. This is especially apparent in their fighting styles -- Altair, Ezio, and the rest of the PC assassins are all proficient in all four combat abilities, using hand-to-hand combat, crossbows, throwing knives, grenades, all sorts of melee weapons, firearms, and occasionally even siege weapons as the situation requires. While a Night-caste Solar could simulate an Assassin's stealth and larceny talents they would be hard-pressed to achieve this kind of flexibility, while a Lunar with an arsenal of dexterity charms can apply them and her Dexterity Excellency to any piece of kit she might come across.<br /> <br /> The one and only sticking point here is the lack of shapeshifting powers among the order. Even so the Assassins have long had a bird of prey motif, what with the peaked hoods and Eagle Vision powers which can undoubtedly be modeled by Perception charms. Connor also has some sort of affinity for wolves, to the point of commanding them as minions in the Tyranny of King Washington DLC if memory serves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T20:10:15-08:00","id":406306,"title":"","content":"I'll admit, when I first went off to assassinate Ben Franklin with my magical native American powers, &quot;Lunar&quot; was not what I thought of first. However, now that you mention it, the Power of Wolf, Bear, and Eagle could be charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T20:18:02-08:00","id":406310,"title":"","content":"I honestly can't see any of the Assassins being a Lunar at all, even Conner. They're all textbook Solar Nights, maybe Sidereals if we wanted to go with a Chosen of Endings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T20:25:03-08:00","id":406311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/406277-assassin-s-creed-ideal-lunar-inspiration?p=406310#post406310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly can't see any of the Assassins being a Lunar at all, even Conner. They're all textbook Solar Nights, maybe Sidereals if we wanted to go with a Chosen of Endings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Textbook Nights wouldn't invest in every combat ability save for War.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T20:30:57-08:00","id":406313,"title":"","content":"No, they invest in melee, and put a dot and a charm or two in the others, because 90% of the time you're swinging around a weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T20:56:51-08:00","id":406323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/406277-assassin-s-creed-ideal-lunar-inspiration?p=406313#post406313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they invest in melee, and put a dot and a charm or two in the others, because 90% of the time you're swinging around a weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>One or two dots isn't sufficient to describe the way throwing knives and crossbow bolts are nearly always one-hit kills, or how Edward can fire four shots and kill four targets casually with his bandoleer of pistols, or the huge variety in unarmed kill moves. That's superhuman skill in every category, and you don't get that without excellencies and reasonably deep charm investment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T21:21:49-08:00","id":406333,"title":"","content":"Naw, an Excellency, and two or three charms at most is typically enough to take care of that if you factor in stealth charms that let you launch a surprise attack every round. Especially when most of the people who you fight as any of the Assassins are extras at who you can onshot as a matter of course once you get a high enough ability score.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T21:37:11-08:00","id":406340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/406277-assassin-s-creed-ideal-lunar-inspiration?p=406333#post406333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Naw, an Excellency, and two or three charms at most is typically enough to take care of that if you factor in stealth charms that let you launch a surprise attack every round. Especially when most of the people who you fight as any of the Assassins are extras at who you can onshot as a matter of course once you get a high enough ability score.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is great so long as you aren't trying to adapt them for use in Creation, where you need to worry about things like dragonbloods and other targets that don't go squish when you give them a mean look.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T21:39:45-08:00","id":406341,"title":"","content":"Yeah, those targets you use your Melee charms on, which you have a much higher investment in than the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T21:48:47-08:00","id":406342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/406277-assassin-s-creed-ideal-lunar-inspiration?p=406341#post406341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, those targets you use your Melee charms on, which you have a much higher investment in than the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>At which point you're not playing like an Assassin anymore because you aren't able to approach your targets with a great deal of flexibility. Being able to use all weapons equally-well is critical to the build.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T21:55:05-08:00","id":406343,"title":"","content":"Not really, I played though those games using the ranged weapons they gave you maybe.... once or twice every other mission? Even then it was usually just to take out a guard or whoever might have spotted me. 90% of the time it was just melee, especially when they force you to fight a bunch of dudes all at once. Mostly your other weapon become tools to get you to areas, rather than weapons you rely on.<br /> <br /> Really, if you want to port over an Assassin in to Creation, make a Solar and put some dots in War so you can get those Omni-excellency combat charms, then put the bulk of your XP in stealth, melee, athletics and awareness. Maybe Larceny if you want to mix it up a bit. After that you should spend XP on backgrounds (assassin order) and any other ability charms that you feel might be useful.<br /> <br /> EDIT: this is for 2.5E, though, where specialization for Solars is really important. In 3E I keep hearing about how diversification is something to be encouraged for Solars, so you can probably spread your dots and charms around and function just as well, if not better than your 2.5E incarnation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 02-15-2015, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T22:15:16-08:00","id":406367,"title":"","content":"As a Lunar, you'd get close to people and kill them in entirely different ways. Shapeshifting is such an incredibly useful tool for an assassin, that it would completely change the way you spy on people and assassinate them. I say this from experience of playing a No Moon Lunar. For getting around, it's not dexterity charms you use, it's turning into a bird/fly/cat/different person. Doing it in your own human form just enhanced by charms... yeah, you really want to play a Solar.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say, if you want to play a Lunar based on Assassin's Creed, you can't. Go for it! I just think you'd quickly find that you'll be doing things entirely different.<br /> Though, why you'd want to play a Lunar based on the boring assassins from that game rather than a drugged-up teenage Ismaili who believes they've been to Heaven already and are fanatically willing to die because they think it'll be back to the place they went before, with all the delicious food and sexy ladies (and, most importantly, where they were high as balls), I don't know. But that's your choice.<br /> Or an actual historical assassin (who didn't really smoke hash, that's just what Marco Polo heard).<br /> <br /> I will say that fighting with a wide array of weapons, as you seem keen on, does work well with Lunars, because as you say, all your Dex charms cross-apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-15-2015, 01:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T00:46:08-08:00","id":406492,"title":"","content":"Yeah the assassins seem like a night caste who went battle hydra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T01:45:26-08:00","id":406505,"title":"","content":"Not textbook Nights, but repeated instances of a particular <i>kind</i> of Night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T02:53:11-08:00","id":406534,"title":"","content":"I want Lunars to have the same sense of freedom I did while playing Creed. Flowing over rooftops, blending into crowds, knowing you have a half dozen ways to escape the city without being caught.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T03:55:10-08:00","id":406555,"title":"","content":"Filtered through Tobuscus' literal trailers (my real introduction to the series) it's hard for me not to see the Assassins as Abyssals since they come across as killing machines who occasionally sneak around.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kKrtbUinWOU\" data-code=\"kKrtbUinWOU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/kKrtbUinWOU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T08:59:32-08:00","id":406737,"title":"","content":"I dunno, I could see Assassin's Creed being a Lunar thing:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img537/3462/s9Tjuy.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Obviously some freaky ass shapeshifting going on there.<br /> <br /> And also the Assassins are all Sidereals, based on the fact that every one of them quite obviously has Arcane Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T09:41:34-08:00","id":406790,"title":"","content":"I could see them being Sidereals. Their primary storyline is about them manipulating humanity behind the scenes towards a future that they think is best, which is pretty much the Sidereal MO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T10:09:48-08:00","id":406805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/406277-assassin-s-creed-ideal-lunar-inspiration?p=406790#post406790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see them being Sidereals. Their primary storyline is about them manipulating humanity behind the scenes towards a future that they think is best, which is pretty much the Sidereal MO.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the Templars. The Assassins spend all their time <i>tearing down</i> people who try to manipulate humanity. Templars also almost always operate from a position of strength in the local government, which fits the Siddies using the Realm as their collective finger puppet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T10:09:52-08:00","id":406806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/406277-assassin-s-creed-ideal-lunar-inspiration?p=406534#post406534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want Lunars to have the same sense of freedom I did while playing Creed. Flowing over rooftops, blending into crowds, knowing you have a half dozen ways to escape the city without being caught.</div> </div> </div> </div>While not challenging the validity of your experience, I think you should ALSO look into Youtube videos of EVOLvE game-matches from the monster-player's point of view for a taste of the Lunar Vs Wyld Hunt experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T10:51:49-08:00","id":406841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/406277-assassin-s-creed-ideal-lunar-inspiration?p=406805#post406805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the Templars. The Assassins spend all their time <i>tearing down</i> people who try to manipulate humanity. Templars also almost always operate from a position of strength in the local government, which fits the Siddies using the Realm as their collective finger puppet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only half the time, the other half the time it's the assassins who are calling the shots, as the war was a very back and forth thing. Either way though, you play a hyper lethal assassin, and sneaking and infiltration to core to the themes of being an assassin. Both the Sidereal and Solars have Castes that let them be a dedicated sneaky/killy guy, where as the Lunars just have shapeshifting that coincidentally lets them infiltrate if they happen to have the right forms for it. The assassins work better as Nights fighting The Realm or a Ronin Sidereal, not a Lunar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T12:31:15-08:00","id":406886,"title":"","content":"I've developed this idea of Destiny engineering being a bit like using the Animus, just where the idea is about synchronizing with the future rather than the past in order to make progress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T19:09:27-08:00","id":407253,"title":"","content":"So, I only played the beginning of the first game...<br /> I assume the series ends with the Assassins framing the Templars for being satanist Muslim witches who have giant gay orgies all the time? Or is that just the first game?<br /> <br /> I could definitely imagine Lunars doing that to a local Immaculate Monastery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T20:06:39-08:00","id":407294,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jnk15Wf6xMU\" target=\"_blank\">Oh, there's definitely some Lunar shennanigans going on in Assassin's Creed.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T20:32:56-08:00","id":407336,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think you could model the Assassins in a couple of different ways. Lunars fits well with their adaptability, and I feel the need to remind people that shapeshifting is not all the Lunars do. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, Solar could also work well, although you'd be taking the more Ezio approach with Solars (who can have animal motifs themselves).<br /> <br /> Basically, Connor's the biggest Assassins-as-Lunars inspiration, while Ezio's the Assassins-as-Solars inspiration IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T21:42:45-08:00","id":407381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/406277-assassin-s-creed-ideal-lunar-inspiration?p=407294#post407294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jnk15Wf6xMU\" target=\"_blank\">Oh, there's definitely some Lunar shennanigans going on in Assassin's Creed.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Kittens and superior Solar familiars, confirmed Goddamned that was adorable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T04:27:29-08:00","id":407579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/406277-assassin-s-creed-ideal-lunar-inspiration?p=407253#post407253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume the series ends with the Assassins framing the Templars for being satanist Muslim witches who have giant gay orgies all the time? Or is that just the first game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Assassin's Creed's mythology breaks down severely if you try to match the groups as they're portrayed in the series with actual historical events and philosophies.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T10:48:27-08:00","id":407945,"title":"","content":"I assumed so, I was being facetious. I seriously doubted an American-made game would have the heroes shout &quot;Allah Akbar!&quot; every time something good happened.<br /> <br /> Still, it's not like no-one else has ever made up stories about the Templars that had very little to do with the real order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T12:32:12-08:00","id":408063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/406277-assassin-s-creed-ideal-lunar-inspiration?p=407253#post407253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I only played the beginning of the first game...<br /> I assume the series ends with the Assassins framing the Templars for being satanist Muslim witches who have giant gay orgies all the time? Or is that just the first game?<br /> <br /> I could definitely imagine Lunars doing that to a local Immaculate Monastery.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's the opening of the most recent game. You're playing as one of the Templars trying to defend their headquarters from French, Papal, and Assassin forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T18:06:15-08:00","id":408393,"title":"","content":"Poor templars. I think it teaches us a valuable lesson though: if you want people to like you, don't become bankers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T18:28:15-08:00","id":408403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/406277-assassin-s-creed-ideal-lunar-inspiration?p=408393#post408393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Poor templars. I think it teaches us a valuable lesson though: if you want people to like you, don't become bankers.</div> </div> </div> </div>When has that ever not been true? Hell, look how many religions call <i>charging interest on a loan</i> out as a sin. Likewise, the ratio of bad bankers to good bankers in movies is way out of proportion.<br /> <br /> Even the spirit &quot;friends on the other side&quot; from whom Doctor Facilier draws his power in <i>The Princess and the Frog</i> give him that magic at interest as part of a scheme to grab up everything, and when the protagonists of the movie break his magic doodad, they drag him, screaming and begging, into hell for being unable to pay his debts - incidentally, as a person with student loan debt, I found that to be a very chilling scene\u2026 it was very much a movie where I sympathized with the &quot;villain.&quot; &gt;.&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-16-2015, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T19:54:27-08:00","id":408525,"title":"","content":"I feel about the same on that, and for similar reasons.<br /> <br /> That said, there's some inspiration there for Cecelyne X Ebon Dragon charms in the Friends on the Other Side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T22:22:50-08:00","id":408619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/406277-assassin-s-creed-ideal-lunar-inspiration?p=408403#post408403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> incidentally, as a person with student loan debt, I found that to be a very chilling scene\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I didn't know innocent souls were accepted currency.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T10:22:40-08:00","id":409083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/406277-assassin-s-creed-ideal-lunar-inspiration?p=408619#post408619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? I didn't know innocent souls were accepted currency.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The American economy has gotten really rough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T18:24:54-08:00","id":409472,"title":"","content":"Innocent? We're talking about a student here. I'm a university teacher, believe me, students are not innocent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T22:18:32-08:00","id":409675,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, a humanities degree is bullshit. My English bachelor's degree and Journalism masters are basically really expensive toilet paper.<br /> <br /> Anyone who hasn't already, don't bother going to college unless you've already looked at the requirements for the job you want, and they list a specific degree you can get at a college you can afford.<br /> <br /> I spent so much money and so many years, and it's basically gotten me nothing. Work experience is what really matters, so being an intern would have been a better investment than being a student.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T22:27:02-08:00","id":409682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/406277-assassin-s-creed-ideal-lunar-inspiration?p=409675#post409675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, a humanities degree is bullshit. My English bachelor's degree and Journalism masters are basically really expensive toilet paper.<br /> <br /> Anyone who hasn't already, don't bother going to college unless you've already looked at the requirements for the job you want, and they list a specific degree you can get at a college you can afford.<br /> <br /> I spent so much money and so many years, and it's basically gotten me nothing. Work experience is what really matters, so being an intern would have been a better investment than being a student.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that in many cases, you have to be a student to get an internship. Or any consideration for a job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T22:36:10-08:00","id":409690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/406277-assassin-s-creed-ideal-lunar-inspiration?p=409682#post409682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that in many cases, you have to be a student to get an internship. Or any consideration for a job.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to take you word for it; I was a full-time student and never an intern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T22:47:09-08:00","id":409707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anubisxy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#2379B5\">Oh, there's definitely some Lunar shennanigans going on in Assassin's Creed.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Pretty Kitty Revolution FTW!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/406277-assassin-s-creed-ideal-lunar-inspiration?p=409675#post409675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, a humanities degree is bullshit. My English bachelor's degree and Journalism masters are basically really expensive toilet paper.<br /> <br /> Anyone who hasn't already, don't bother going to college unless you've already looked at the requirements for the job you want, and they list a specific degree you can get at a college you can afford.<br /> <br /> I spent so much money and so many years, and it's basically gotten me nothing. Work experience is what really matters, so being an intern would have been a better investment than being a student.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gods above and below, I wish someone had explained this to me years ago...Furthermore, I would caution you to, honestly, take a break for a year or so after HS, don't just enroll just because it's &quot;the next step in education&quot; that you &quot;have to&quot; take. Take a year or so to work or travel, just to figure out what you *really* want to study...IF you really want to go at all! I know it can seem hard trying to explain to your parents, esp if they've saved for you all those years and believe you need to get cracking on that degree to be successful, but it's *not their lives, it's yours*, and they should respect that. Anyway, if they held onto all that money for this long, one more year or so shouldn't make a difference...<br /> <br /> Hell, even if you do know what you want to do, a degree may not help you do it. I know far too many people with them who are not (and never have) working in the fields they spent all that time and money training for...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T22:59:17-08:00","id":409726,"title":"","content":"Sound advice. Despite long graduating from school, I was thinking of going back to take some classes simply to gain a broader skill set and pick up knowledge that I always wanted but never had cause to pursue. I'll definitely consider what you said when looking at classes, Sunder and Omega.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T23:56:53-08:00","id":409760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/406277-assassin-s-creed-ideal-lunar-inspiration?p=409726#post409726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Despite long graduating from school, I was thinking of going back to take some classes simply to gain a broader skill set and pick up knowledge that I always wanted but never had cause to pursue.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's less-bullshitty ways of learning a skill, though - even if you absolutely want to acquire something that's currently a college course, you'll be way better off buying last year's dirt-cheap &quot;edition&quot; of whatever book they're charging students an arm and a leg for, and reading it yourself, instead of being cornholed by the publishers for the &quot;privilege&quot; of having an untrained guy with maybe five years on you try and &quot;teach&quot; you what you can already find in what's essentially <i>the exact same book</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-18-2015, 03:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T00:20:00-08:00","id":409771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/406277-assassin-s-creed-ideal-lunar-inspiration?p=409707#post409707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, I would caution you to, honestly, take a break for a year or so after HS, don't just enroll just because it's &quot;the next step in education&quot; that you &quot;have to&quot; take. Take a year or so to work or travel, just to figure out what you *really* want to study...IF you really want to go at all! I know it can seem hard trying to explain to your parents, esp if they've saved for you all those years and believe you need to get cracking on that degree to be successful, but it's *not their lives, it's yours*, and they should respect that. Anyway, if they held onto all that money for this long, one more year or so shouldn't make a difference...</div> </div> </div> </div>After my brother and I graduated college and went into the AmeriCorp program, Mom said she wished she'd pushed us to do AmeriCorp FIRST, THEN college.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T00:23:30-08:00","id":409772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/406277-assassin-s-creed-ideal-lunar-inspiration?p=409760#post409760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's less-bullshitty ways of learning a skill, though - even if you absolutely want to acquire something that's currently a college course, you'll be way better off buying last year's dirt-cheap &quot;edition&quot; of whatever book they're charging students an arm and a leg for, and reading it yourself, instead of being cornholed by the publishers for the &quot;privilege&quot; of having an untrained guy with maybe five years on you try and &quot;teach&quot; you what you can already find in what's essentially <i>the exact same book</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll consider it, my problem is that my self-education attempts are somewhat rocky, but saving money is definitely nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T01:04:39-08:00","id":411182,"title":"","content":"Not to end the topic change but, I have to say this thread is probably the best example of the origin of my contempt for Lunars as the shapeshifter / animal Exalted, and Solars as the &quot;does things&quot; exalted. Because they seem to prevent the community from saying &quot;my first instinct would be Night caste but I can see a Lunar&quot; in favour of &quot;the assassins do things and don't shapeshift, that means they're not Lunars (because they don't shapeshift) and are Solars (because they do things)!&quot;<br /> <br /> It'd be so much nicer if we didn't feel the need to be &quot;right&quot; over being enthusiastic. I suppose the original poster may have been &quot;asking for it&quot; by daring to suggest a cool awesome character could be inspiration for anything other than a Solar but still, the community could really stand to realize that &quot;x can be used as inspiration for y&quot; does not outlaw, contradict, detract from, or diminish the standard answer of &quot;anything is an inspiration for Solars&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":".  Fixing typographical errors from phone. 02-19-2015, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}